C# Strings – Part 1: Members of the string Class-
------------------------------------------------

Why Is This Important?-
---------------------
The string class in C# comes with built-in members (properties and methods) that make it easy to:

Measure the text

Convert cases (uppercase/lowercase)

Remove extra spaces

Check if a string contains a word

Validate user input


1).Length – To Get Number of Characters
--------
string name = "Venkatesh";
Console.WriteLine(name.Length);  // Output: 9

.Length gives total characters (including spaces).


 2).ToUpper()-Convert to Uppercase
 ------------
 
string city = "bangalore";
Console.WriteLine(city.ToUpper()); // Output: BANGALORE

3).ToLower()-Convert to Lowercase
    ----------- 
string title = "Trainer";
Console.WriteLine(title.ToLower()); // Output: trainer

4).Trim() – Removes Extra Spaces
---------
string name = "  Venkatesh  ";
Console.WriteLine(name.Trim());  // Output: "Venkatesh"

Useful when you take user input and want to clean it.

5).Contains() – Check If Word Exists
-------------
string message = "Welcome to Bangalore";
Console.WriteLine(message.Contains("Bangalore")); // true
Console.WriteLine(message.Contains("Hyderabad")); // false

6).StartsWith() and .EndsWith()
---------------

string code = "CSHARP101";
Console.WriteLine(code.StartsWith("CS"));  // true
Console.WriteLine(code.EndsWith("101"));   // true


 Full Example Program: Practice All Together-
 ------------------------------------------
 
using System;

class StringMembersDemo
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string course = "  CSharp Full Stack  ";

        Console.WriteLine("Length: " + course.Length);               // includes spaces
        Console.WriteLine("Trimmed: [" + course.Trim() + "]");      // removes front/back spaces
        Console.WriteLine("Uppercase: " + course.ToUpper());        // CSHARP FULL STACK
        Console.WriteLine("Lowercase: " + course.ToLower());        // csharp full stack
        Console.WriteLine("Contains 'Full': " + course.Contains("Full"));  // true
        Console.WriteLine("StartsWith 'CSharp': " + course.Trim().StartsWith("CSharp")); // true
        Console.WriteLine("EndsWith 'Stack': " + course.Trim().EndsWith("Stack"));       // true
    }
}


